<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 54.9 percent of their intended 3.8 million hectares of 1996/97 maize by November 1, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Sunflower sowing reached 41.2 percent of 3.0 million hectares, which would be 12.1 percent lower than last season's area. Area sown with soybeans should be between 3.0 and 5.0 percent more than last season. Wheat harvesting reached 0.7 percent of the total 6.9 million hectares, which is 36 percent more area than in 1995/96. Recent rains have improved the state of the wheat and raised probable yields.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,867  100.0(100.0)    84.0    0.7   (n/a)   (13.2)</p>
<p> Maize     3,780   54.9 (59.3)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans    n/a    n/a  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 2,999   41.2 (48.8)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     774   11.7 (10.8)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	969   18.9  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
